**Declared actions.** This step MUST do exactly these, and the worker base prompt says what each verb obliges:
- `DELETE_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentCollectionProxyTests -> OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentCollectionRoundTripTests`

**How to implement.** The constructor works inside a kit: it holds a `KitContext` in place of the collection seam, and committing, editing and removing an experiment write and delete its kit file (001 §S4 'today's experiments and scenes persist into the kit'; 001 §R; the S4.3 brief; .spec-md §0.1 `TableAndElementRotationView.fs` 'Hosts a KitContext in place of the scene and collection seams'). The windows work in their scratch kit until step 154 opens a picked folder. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/ExperimentCollectionStore.fs`: `ExperimentCollectionProxy` and its `createInMemory` extension (`ExperimentCollectionStore.fs:ExperimentCollectionProxy`), `ExperimentCollectionError` and `CollectionName.tryCreate` are deleted, because nothing saves, lists or loads a named collection any more. `CollectionName` (with `.value`) and `ExperimentCollectionSnapshot` stay: they are the collection the solver hand-off shows (`SolverHandoffView.fs:SolverHandoffContext`), which S11.5 retires. The module doc becomes one to three lines saying so (spec 0050 S4.3), every doc sentence naming the proxy, `Scene.SceneProxy`, a future store or `.ocproj` goes, and the comment above its `<Compile>` in `OpticalConstructor.Domain.fsproj` is cut to the words that stay true. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`. (a) `TableAndElementRotationModel` (`TableAndElementRotationView.fs:TableAndElementRotationModel`) loses `experimentCollections`, `collectionName`, `savedCollections` and `collectionStatus`, and gains `kit : KitContext` (the kit the constructor works in) and `kitStatus : ControlCaption option` (the last kit read or write that needs telling), each with a one-line doc; `experimentData`'s doc says it reads through `kit`. The `open OpticalConstructor.Domain.ExperimentCollectionStore` and its comment go. (b) `defaultExperimentProxies` is deleted. `initWith` loses its `experimentData` and `experimentCollections` parameters: it sets `kit` to `KitOpening.scratchKit ()` (step 150), `experimentData` to `ExperimentDataStore.createFileBacked` over that kit's proxy (step 135) and `kitStatus` to `None`. `initTableAndElementRotation`, `initMainWith`, `initInverse` and `initMain` keep their signatures and stop passing the two proxies. (c) `type TableAndElementRotationModel with member model.loadKit (opened : OpenedKit) : TableAndElementRotationModel` (step 150), its doc one to three lines: the model working in an opened kit. It sets `kit` to `opened.library.kit`, `experimentData` to `opened.experimentData`, `experimentCollection` to `Experiments.ExperimentCollection.ofLoaded opened.experiments` (`Experiments.fs:ExperimentCollection`) and `kitStatus` to `None`, and computes `experimentDataStatus` as step 136's `CollectionLoad` arm did: one status per loaded experiment with an attachment, through `experimentData.attachmentStatus` and the one private validation function, moved here unchanged, so a changed or missing data file is flagged when the kit opens (001 §E). (d) Writing through the kit. The kit's library is `{ kit = model.kit; imports = model.catalogueImports }` (steps 101, 139). `ExpCommit` computes the committed collection as today; when the draft committed (the collection changed), the experiment the draft now edits (`draft.editingId`, `Experiments.fs:commit`) is recorded through `recordExperiment` (step 149): on `Ok` the model takes the new collection and `kitStatus` is `None`; on `Error e` the model keeps its collection and `kitStatus` is `Some (ControlCaption $"Not saved to the kit — {e.describe}")`. `ExpRemove id` calls `model.kit.proxy.deleteExperiment id` (step 148): `Ok` or `MissingKitFileErr` removes the experiment (its file is gone either way); any other error keeps it and sets `kitStatus` the same way. `AttachDataFileTo` (step 135): the experiment carrying its new attachment is recorded through `recordExperiment` before the model takes it; on an error the experiment keeps what it had, its data status is unchanged, and `kitStatus` names the error. `ExpEdit`, `ExpNew` and the draft messages write nothing. (e) `CollectionSetName`, `CollectionSave` and `CollectionLoad` (`TableAndElementRotationView.fs:TableAndElementRotationMsg`) and their arms are deleted. (f) `collectionBuilderView` loses its name field, Save button, status line and saved list. It shows `kitStatus`, when `Some`, in a wrapping `TextBlock` carrying `ConstructorUiId.kitStatus`, and then the inverse `Data files:` section unchanged. Its doc and the section comment above it say the experiments are kept in the kit; every comment that names the collection store, `SceneProxy` or `.experimentCollections` names the kit. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs`: `collectionNameField`, `saveCollectionButton` and `savedCollections` (`UiIds.fs:165-168`) are deleted, and `collectionStatus` becomes `kitStatus` (`"KitStatus"`) under a doc line naming the kit status line and the data files. `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs`: `ConstructorUiId.savedCollection` (`ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs:70`) and the `CollectionName.caption` extension (`:250`) are deleted. (4) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/AppContext.fs`: `experimentData` and `experimentCollections` (`AppContext.fs:AppContext`) and their composition go, because the measured-data seam reads through the kit a window works in; the record doc names what remains. (5) `OpticalConstructor.App/Program.fs`: `MainConstructorWindow` and `InverseConstructorWindow` stop threading `experimentData` and `experimentCollections`, and their docs and `ConstructorScene`'s stop naming the collection store. (6) Tests. `OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentCollectionProxyTests.fs` is deleted with its `<Compile>` entry and comment; its five facts test the deleted proxy and `CollectionName.tryCreate`, and step 148's kit-file facts in `ExperimentCollectionRoundTripTests` cover what the store did. The `OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj` comment above `ExperimentCollectionRoundTripTests.fs` names the kit files, and that file's doc names no proxy. (a) `TestAppScope` (step 83) gains, each with a one-line doc citing .spec-md §3.10: `freshKitFolder (owner : FolderName) : KitFolder`, a new GUID-named folder under `testLocations owner`'s `kitsFolder`, not created; and `openedKitIn (owner : FolderName) (imports : CatalogueImportContext) : OpenedKit`, `KitOpening.openKitAt` (step 150) over `freshKitFolder owner` read-write with `ClockProvider.system` and `KitAuthor "test"`, failing the calling fact with the error's `describe` otherwise. (b) `InverseConstructorTests`: `inverse ()` is `initInverse` over the class's stores, then `loadKit (TestAppScope.openedKitIn (FolderName "InverseConstructorTests") m.catalogueImports)`, so its facts run over a folder kit; the mocks are set by record update after it, and every fact keeps its assertions. `a named collection round-trips through save, list, and load` becomes `committed experiments and their attachments are kept in the kit and reopen with it`: after the commit and the attach of `withIntensityExperiment`, `readExperiments` of the model's kit answers the model's experiments, and, the kit closed, an inverse model loaded from `openKitAt` of the same folder holds equal experiments with the attachment. `saving a collection with a blank name reports a typed status and stores nothing` and `loading an unknown collection reports a typed status and leaves the live collection alone` are deleted with the collection builder; step 153's scene facts cover a blank name and a miss. Step 136's `loading a collection re-validates an attachment whose data is unchanged` and `loading a collection flags an attachment whose data changed since attach or is missing` become `opening a kit re-validates an attachment whose data is unchanged` and `opening a kit flags an attachment whose data changed since attach or is missing`: the experiments are written into a folder kit, the kit opened through `openKitAt`, and the model loaded through `loadKit` of that opened kit with the mock as its `experimentData`, with the same assertions. It gains `a commit, an attach and a removal write the kit's experiment files`: a commit writes `E1.experiment-json`, the attach rewrites it with the attachment, and `ExpRemove` deletes it and drops the experiment; and `a kit write that fails keeps the experiment and shows why`: over a model whose kit is its own kit's read-only view (`{ m.kit with proxy = m.kit.proxy.readOnlyView; access = ReadOnlyKitAccess }`), `ExpCommit` leaves the collection as it was and `kitStatus` holds `KitReadOnlyErr`'s text. `the inverse workbench renders the collection builder without throwing` drops its two collection messages and keeps rendering. (c) `AppContextTests.surfaceOf` drops its two record-update fields. (d) `WireUiFinalCompositionTests`: `the finalized app scope carries every store proxy — the step-027 scene seam is composed at the root` is deleted, because the app scope composes no scene or experiment store and `AppContextTests`' `create carries the settings record it was given, verbatim` pins its settings; the solver hand-off its factory opens reads through `ExperimentDataStore.createFileBacked (KitOpening.scratchKit ()).proxy`; its module doc and the `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.fsproj` comments naming `ExperimentCollectionProxy` say the kit. (e) `SolverHandoffWindowTests.baseExperiment` sets its model's `catalogueImports` to `(TestAppScope.freshAppContext (FolderName "SolverHandoffWindowTests")).catalogueImports`, a library holding the presets it binds, so its commit records them; every fact keeps its assertions. After this step `git grep -n -E "SceneProxy|ExperimentCollectionProxy" -- Berreman/` finds nothing.

**Acceptance.** After the constructor holds its kit, `TableAndElementRotationModel` MUST hold `kit` and no collection store, a commit, an attach and a removal MUST write and delete the experiment's kit file (a failed write keeping the experiment and showing `kitStatus`), `loadKit` MUST flag changed and missing data, and `git grep -n -E "SceneProxy|ExperimentCollectionProxy" -- Berreman/` MUST find nothing; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, the count falling by 5; ui-smoke MUST pass, including `the inverse workbench renders the collection builder without throwing`; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `committed experiments and their attachments are kept in the kit and reopen with it`, `opening a kit re-validates an attachment whose data is unchanged`, `opening a kit flags an attachment whose data changed since attach or is missing`, `a commit, an attach and a removal write the kit's experiment files`, `a kit write that fails keeps the experiment and shows why`, the count falling by 1; and build, elevation and the eleven s17 invariants MUST pass.
